{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: recover the remaining oversized-attachment outcome of #137. Queue after the existing work through #20084; preserve current landing/review work and every earlier commitment. #137's reference-check and back-pressure outcomes are delivered and are not being reopened.\n\nThe [audit evidence](kernel-admission-recovery.json) records the original three conditions, actual merge ancestry and current passing tests for the first two, the satisfied projection, Hugh's still-unretired but stale decision #5075 and its effective ratification, and your #7447 finding that the third outcome remained unimplemented. You confirmed no later implementation or authorized narrowing is known. A merge of the reference-check subset closed the old commitment without settling the locator outcome.\n\nAt the examined head, [signRequest](internal/app/app.go@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:1955) signs the supplied attachment tree, [the kernel](internal/kernel/kernel.go@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:471) hard-refuses the aggregate genesis ceiling, and [the limits guide](docs/reference/limits.md@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:25) documents that bound. The old [design](notes/2026-08-05-gitseq-design.md@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:115) still describes a reference path. [Evidence previews](internal/service/preview.go@50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591:99) now exist, so #7447's unreadable-on-arrival premise no longer holds. This audit did not measure current demand and does not prescribe adding a feature regardless of value.\n\nBring this remaining outcome to one explicit, current disposition: implement the adopted locator-required/no-implicit-custody policy, or obtain an authorized narrowing that retains the hard ceiling and deliver the agreed refusal guidance and consistent documentation. Start with a bounded current assessment of actual attachment sizes/use, reachable input surfaces, how readers would show a descriptor, and the smallest useful option. Do not convert a lack of replies or a design-only merge into completion. The governing decision is stale before this follow-on begins: prepare one concrete proposal for ordinary Gitseq ratifier adoption on current bases before implementation/formal design review, per SKILL.md; planner cannot adopt it as Hugh here. Explain what would change from #5075 if recommending narrowing. Keep explanatory alternatives outside the proposal's one ratifiable outcome.\n\nIf the locator path is adopted: convert and validate before signing in the application; preserve the kernel ceiling and signed payload binding; require an explicit locator, store no external bytes implicitly, and do not fetch or execute a locator automatically. Define a versioned, bounded inert descriptor, digest/object-format meaning and custody/availability limits, invalid/colliding names, multiple attachments and aggregate signed-envelope accounting. Keep one idempotency key through any measure/re-sign step, deterministic retries and explicit refusal when no locator is supplied. Expose the supported CLI/MCP inputs and understandable descriptor/preview state through the current reading surface; unavailable external bytes must never appear verified or held by Gitseq. Do not weaken admission, resource bounds or existing inline evidence.\n\nIf narrowing is adopted: retain explicit safe refusal, improve its actionable diagnostic as agreed, correct the original design claim and current guides, and record the ratifier's actual abandonment of conversion. In either case run focused positive/refusal and omission controls for the chosen behavior, including aggregate envelope boundary and retry/no-append guarantees where affected; record architecture, security and simplification conclusions in independent exact-head review. Publish exact changed paths, ratify the independent verdict, seal/push the final landing and workroom/receipt refs, check main CI, and remove the owned branch/worktree. Keep this commitment open through the full selected outcome; if an intermediate design must land separately, ask planner to file the stage request before that partial landing so the remaining delivery stays assigned.\n\nNo genesis change, live migration, external storage provisioning, automatic URL access, key operation, resident restart or deployment is part of this request.","body":{"branch":"request/oversized-attachment-disposition","conditions":"Resolve only the remaining third outcome of #137 through the full selected delivery described in this request: current bounded assessment and one explicit ordinary ratifier adoption, then either the locator-required/no-implicit-custody path or an authorized hard-ceiling narrowing with its refusal and documentation work. Preserve signed aggregate limits, retry identity, no automatic fetching and honest custody/preview semantics. Independent exact-head architecture/security/simplification review and relevant positive/refusal/omission gates; sealed exact-path publication, push, main CI and owned-worktree cleanup. A design-only or partial landing does not satisfy this whole request; assign any remaining stage before that landing. Queue after existing work through #20084; no live operations.","head":"50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f3ceaff591","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a0c1f08bff46a3ce1e4cfca5ef4b108a72405bf4, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:fcb32a61ec6415eda5d909b4db7e215a07c1dc8a stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:015aba51ab6c2416861618c5ac3c9ae0e444f17f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:03270b167c8f14b55a31919b2489715ee513b20f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:092bd6cbe60056cd85ba626ea22807c1e97cc376, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b8a9ff517318daec88e265b848e08ea877e98fa and 51 more","target_head":"50850a358d01666fe19c85007aed98f